  "identifier": "batchgenerators",
  "name": "batchgenerators",
  "description": "Framework-agnostic Python data augmentation library for 2D and 3D medical imaging. Provides spatial transforms (elastic deformations, rotations, scaling, mirroring), intensity augmentations (gamma, brightness, contrast), noise injection, and anatomy-informed operations compatible with both PyTorch and TensorFlow training pipelines. Handles volumetric (3D) data natively — a differentiator from most general-purpose augmentation libraries. Used as the augmentation backend in nnU-Net but widely adopted independently for medical image segmentation and classification training. Apache 2.0, 1.2k stars, v0.25.1 (March 2024). A successor, batchgeneratorsv2, is in active development (February 2025). Developed at MIC-DKFZ / Helmholtz Imaging.",
  "url": "https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/batchgenerators",
