  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The de facto data augmentation library for medical image segmentation training — 1.2k stars, Apache 2.0, pip-installable, framework-agnostic. Core augmentation backend of nnU-Net (already in the MACH catalog) and widely adopted independently across medical imaging research pipelines. Native 3D support is a key differentiator over general-purpose augmentation libraries. Actively maintained by DKFZ with a v2 successor in development. Essential dependency for any team training segmentation models on volumetric medical imaging data.",
